Sure, here's the translation of the text into UML code:

```plantuml
@startuml
actor "Security Team" as SecurityTeam

participant "Security Architect" as Architect
participant "Security Engineer" as Engineer
participant "Manager" as Manager
participant "Scrum Master" as ScrumMaster

SecurityTeam --> Architect : Requires
SecurityTeam --> Engineer : Requires
SecurityTeam --> Manager : Requires
SecurityTeam --> ScrumMaster : Requires

note right of Architect
  Cannot be the same person as\nSecurity Engineer
end note

@enduml
```

This UML diagram represents the requirements for the security team, including the distinct roles of the security architect, security engineer, manager, and scrum master. The note indicates that the security architect and security engineer cannot be the same person.